<section class="section">
  <div class="container is-max-desktop">

    <!-- What is a causal intervention? -->
    <div class="columns is-centered">
      <div class="column is-full-width">
        <h2 class="title is-3">InPhyRe: A Benchmark to Evaluate
        Inductive Physical Reasoning</h2>
        <div class="content has-text-justified">
          <p>
            InPhyRe is designed to carefully evaluate the on-the-fly
            physical reasoning in LMMs, including physical biases in
            LMMs. We first generate object trajectories that follow
            custom physics, and then render these objects using Blender.
          </p>
          <div class="columns is-centered">
            <!-- <div class="column is-3 has-text-centered"> -->
            <img src="./static/images/blender-pipeline.png" width="100%"/>
            <!-- </div> -->
            </div>
        </div>
        </div>
        <br/>
        <!--/ Interpolating. -->

      </div>
    </div>
    <!--/ Animation. -->
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container is-max-desktop">

    <!-- What is a causal intervention? -->
    <div class="columns is-centered">
      <div class="column is-full-width">
        <h2 class="title is-3">What are the physical scenarios in InPhyRe?</h2>
        <div class="content has-text-justified">
            <p>
              InPhyRe contains ten scenarios -- 7 impossible physical
              scenarios (called irregular scenarios),
              and 3 universal physics scenarios (called regular
              scenarios). The categorization of these scenarios is shown below.
            </p>
            <div class="columns is-centered">
            <!-- <div class="column is-3 has-text-centered"> -->
            <img src="./static/images/inphyre-scenarios.png" width="100%"/>
            <!-- </div> -->
            </div>
        </div>
        </div>
        <br/>
        <!--/ Interpolating. -->

      </div>
    </div>
    <!--/ Animation. -->
    </div>
</section>


<section class="hero is-light is-small">
  <div class="hero-body">
    <div class="container">
      <div id="results-carousel" class="carousel results-carousel">

        <div class="item item-coffee">
          <div class="carousel-card">
            <video poster="" id="coffee" autoplay controls muted loop playsinline width="100%">
              <source src="./static/videos/lin_mom_cons.mp4"
                      type="video/mp4">
            </video>
            <div class="carousel-copy">
              <h3>Linear Momentum</h3>
              <p>A moving object collide with an object of equal mass at
              rest. But instead of losing its velocity, the former
              object continues with the same velocity.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="item item-toby">
          <div class="carousel-card">
            <video poster="" id="toby" autoplay controls muted loop playsinline width="100%">
              <source src="./static/videos/ang_mom_cons.mp4"
                      type="video/mp4">
            </video>
            <div class="carousel-copy">
              <h3>Angular Momentum</h3>
              <p>Two objects of equal mass collide head-on, and rotate
              around the center of mass, instead of moving in different
              directions, thus violating angular momentum conservation.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="item item-mask">
          <div class="carousel-card">
            <video poster="" id="mask" autoplay controls muted loop playsinline width="100%">
              <source src="./static/videos/off_the_wall.mp4"
                      type="video/mp4">
            </video>
            <div class="carousel-copy">
              <h3>Off-the-Wall</h3>
              <p>Here, the object collides with a wall on the left side
              and increases its velocity along the vertical direction.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="item item-blueshirt">
          <div class="carousel-card">
            <video poster="" id="blueshirt" autoplay controls muted loop playsinline width="100%">
              <source src="./static/videos/size_bias.mp4"
                      type="video/mp4">
            </video>
            <div class="carousel-copy">
              <h3>Size Bias</h3>
              <p>This scenarios tests whether models over-rely on object
              size cues when predicting motion which should depend
              on mass. Here, a large, low-mass object is deflected after
              colliding with a small, but heavy object.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="item item-fullbody">
          <div class="carousel-card">
            <video poster="" id="fullbody" autoplay controls muted loop playsinline width="100%">
              <source src="./static/videos/color_constancy.mp4"
                      type="video/mp4">
            </video>
            <div class="carousel-copy">
              <h3>Color Constancy</h3>
              <p>A moving object collides with an object rests and assumes
              the appearance (color and shape) of the latter. This
              scenario violates both mechanical laws and object realism.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="item item-shiba">
          <div class="carousel-card">
            <video poster="" id="shiba" autoplay controls muted loop playsinline width="100%">
              <source src="./static/videos/color_lin_mom_cons.mp4"
                      type="video/mp4">
            </video>
            <div class="carousel-copy">
              <h3>Red-LMC</h3>
              <p>Red-colored objects violate linear momentum
              conservation principle after collision, while other object
              satisfy linear momentum conservation. This scenario
              requires conditional inductive physical reasoning.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="item item-chair-tp">
          <div class="carousel-card">
            <video poster="" id="chair-tp" autoplay controls muted loop
            playsinline width="100%">
              <source src="./static/videos/color_passthrough.mp4"
                      type="video/mp4">
            </video>
            <div class="carousel-copy">
              <h3>Red-Pass</h3>
              <p>Red objects can through other objects after collision,
              while the remaining objects follow universal physics. This
              scenario violates both mechanics and realism, and
              evaluates conditional inductive physical reasoning, making
             this one of the most challenging scenarios in InPhyRe.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container is-max-desktop">

    <!-- What is a causal intervention? -->
    <div class="columns is-centered">
      <div class="column is-full-width">
        <h2 class="title is-3">How much parametric knowledge do LMMs
        have about universal physics?</h2>
        <div class="columns is-centered">
          <!-- <div class="column is-3 has-text-centered"> -->
            <img src="./static/images/regular_zero_shot_heatmap.png" class="adaptive-image"/>
          <!-- </div> -->
          </div>
        <div class="content has-text-justified">
        <p style="background-color: #ffd678; padding: 1em;">
          <b>Finding #1</b>: LMMs have limited parametric knowledge
          about the laws of mechanics. Although LMMs can state
          universal laws, they often struggle to apply them for physical reasoning.
        </p>
        </div>
        </div>
        <br/>
        <!--/ Interpolating. -->

      </div>
    </div>
    <!--/ Animation. -->
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container is-max-desktop">

    <!-- What is a causal intervention? -->
    <div class="columns is-centered">
      <div class="column is-full-width">
        <h2 class="title is-3">Can LMMs augment their parametric
        knowledge with demonstration samples?</h2>
        <div class="columns is-centered">
          <!-- <div class="column is-3 has-text-centered"> -->
            <img src="./static/images/regular_few_shot_diff_heatmap.png" class="adaptive-image"/>
          <!-- </div> -->
          </div>
        <div class="content has-text-justified">
          <p style="background-color: #ffd678; padding: 1em;">
          <b>Finding #2</b>: Exemplars that obeyed universal physical
          laws support parametric knowledge in LMMs successfully. This
          is evident from the performance improvement in the above plot. With
          only three exemplars, several LMMs achieve nearly 100%
          prediction accuracy.
        </p>
        </div>
        </div>
        <br/>
        <!--/ Interpolating. -->

      </div>
    </div>
    <!--/ Animation. -->
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container is-max-desktop">

    <!-- What is a causal intervention? -->
    <div class="columns is-centered">
      <div class="column is-full-width">
        <h2 class="title is-3">How strong is inductive physical
        reasoning in LMMs?</h2>
        <div class="columns is-centered">
          <!-- <div class="column is-3 has-text-centered"> -->
            <img src="./static/images/3-shot-video-text.png" class="adaptive-image"/>
          <!-- </div> -->
        </div>
        <div class="content has-text-justified">
          <p style="background-color: #ffd678; padding: 1em;">
          <b>Finding #3</b>: LMMs demonstrate only weak inductive
          physical reasoning when exemplars violate parametric
          knowledge. Almost all LMMs showed significant deterioration in
          performance in the above plot, compared to few-shot regular
          scenario performance.
        </p>
        </div>
        </div>
        <br/>
        <!--/ Interpolating. -->

      </div>
    </div>
    <!--/ Animation. -->
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container is-max-desktop">

    <!-- What is a causal intervention? -->
    <div class="columns is-centered">
      <div class="column is-full-width">
        <h2 class="title is-3">How much of this inductive physical
        reasoning is aided by language?</h2>
        <div class="columns is-centered">
          <!-- <div class="column is-3 has-text-centered"> -->
            <img src="./static/images/3-shot-video-only.png" class="adaptive-image"/>
          <!-- </div> -->
        </div>
        <div class="content has-text-justified">
          <p style="background-color: #ffd678; padding: 1em;">
            <b>Finding #4</b>: Inductive physical reasoning in the
            evaluated LMMs show strong language bias, relying primarily
            on the textual content of the exemplars to answer the
            question. The performance dropped compared to that in few-shot
            irregular scenarios where question-answer pairs were
            provided in demonstration samples.
          </p>
        </div>
        </div>
        <br/>
        <!--/ Interpolating. -->

      </div>
    </div>
    <!--/ Animation. -->
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container is-max-desktop">

    <!-- What is a causal intervention? -->
    <div class="columns is-centered">
      <div class="column is-full-width">
        <h2 class="title is-3">How can we improve inductive physical
        reasoning in LMMs?</h2>
        <div class="content has-text-justified">
          <p>
            We found that explicitly providing the underlying physical
            laws as chain-of-thought prompting improved inductive
            physical reasoning. However, this is not a practical
            solution. A more resilient approach to improve inductive
            physical reasoning is to explicitly embed physics-decoding
            components in LMMs.
          </p>
        </div>
        </div>
        <br/>
        <!--/ Interpolating. -->

      </div>
    </div>
    <!--/ Animation. -->
    </div>
</section>

